  "accepted_intent": [
    "Preserve acknowledged jobs and lease fencing across restarts.",
    "Keep tenant namespaces isolated; synthetic tenant headers are not production authentication.",
    "SQLite WAL and synchronous=FULL remain required; do not trade durability for throughput.",
    "Current source and task contracts govern facts; bounded continuity summaries do not grant authority."
  ],
  "common_prompt": "You own only this disposable QueueForge workspace and its declared private memory\ndata. Implement the requested backend completely; resolve routine details from\nthe contract. Do not inspect parent/sibling projects, evaluator/checker code, other\nconditions or previous outcome summaries. Do not delegate or call another model.\nNo external network/services, credentials, real projects, active plugin changes,\nglobal settings, messages, publishing or deployment. Loopback tests are authorized;\ndependencies are predownloaded and Go module networking is off.\n\nPreserve the supplied driver helper/test and exact go.mod/go.sum. Use Go1.26.3 and\nthe standard library plus the pinned SQLite driver, with no new runtime dependency.\nDo not commit; the coordinator records source commits. Keep owned test processes\nunder this workspace and stop them. Code and development documents are English.\nRead BRIEF.md and current files; do not seek AGENTS outside this workspace.\n\nCurrent source and the task contracts govern facts. Notes/memory retain bounded\npublic intent/progress, never raw prompts, transcripts, code dumps, tool dumps or\nhidden reasoning. A failed continuity operation does not erase constraints or stop\nindependent implementation work. Report actual checks, failures and remaining limits\nin at most800 words. No emitted pack or self-reported completion replaces verification.\n",
